//! task: write
//! ask: Write the canonical Exsecutor program: a public function that returns a greeting and has no authority to do anything else.
//! expect: ok
//! refs: §4.1 rule 6, examples/saluta.exsc
//! explain: The empty row is the point. `publica` with no `poscit` declares that the function observes nothing about the host, so it cannot print: printing is I/O, I/O is authority, and authority is declared. String literals may contain raw newlines (LF only); there is no separate multiline form and no indentation stripping.

publica functio saluta() -> textus {
    redde "Ave, mundus.

Ex silentio surgit forma.
Ex signo nascitur vox.
Ex codice fit lumen.

Hodie incipimus.";
}
